+# R5C External Consumer-Adoption Source and Projection
+
+This ExecPlan is a living document. The sections `Progress`, `Surprises &
+Discoveries`, `Decision Log`, and `Outcomes & Retrospective` must be kept
+current while implementation proceeds.
+
+The repository rules in `.agent/PLANS.md` govern this document.
+
+## Purpose / Big Picture
+
+Agent World currently accepts commandless EventRecords into C2 but has no
+honest path that lets a separate product consumer report its own adoption
+state, lets an independent World preserve that source-scoped authority, and produces a
+source-mapped WorldProjection without inventing a World Command.
+
+This change adds one narrow local-equivalent-real adapter for Allbuddy's
+consumer-adoption source. It does not decide whether the Artifact is correct
+or valuable. It confirms only that the authenticated Allbuddy consumer source
+currently reports `adopted`, `not_adopted`, or `revoked` at a monotonic
+revision.
+
+The only allowed positive conclusion is:
+
+> A synthetic local Allbuddy source reported state X at revision N, and an
+> independent World transport/materialization preserved that scoped report.
+
+The experiment does not establish real customer or human adoption, Artifact
+correctness, execution success, mutual acceptance, business value, actual
+external deployment, actual Harness closure, or production fitness.
+
+A successful demonstration must be visible in three places:
+
+1. the World process has durably persisted the claimed delivery before ack;
+2. C2 contains a commandless, source-authoritative EventRecord with only the
+   coarse readback;
+3. C4 contains one stable projection whose current modifier and Source Map
+   follow the latest accepted revision.
+
+Invalid, unavailable, stale, conflicting, unauthorized or private-content
+responses never advance the adoption business state. After a prior accepted
+state, stale/offline/gap responses explicitly downgrade the last-known claim
+projection to stale/unknown/partial; divergent valid evidence marks it
+disputed. They must not leave an old adopted projection looking current.
+
+## Canonical Basis
+
+This plan is constrained by, and must add closure tests for:
+
+- Semantic Foundation sf-02.7/02.8: Unknown and traceability;
+- sf-13.3: EventRecord observation and source authority;
+- sf-04 and sf-06: claim entities, Unknown and Disputed;
+- sf-13 and sf-24: provenance and correction lineage;
+- sf-31 and sf-32: projection/source-map honesty and non-orphan binding;
+- Product Implementation Blueprint pib-12.2 and 12.16–18: adapter reality,
+  health, partial/offline behavior;
+- pib-13.10: freshness and stale state;
+- pib-16.7: reconciliation;
+- pib-22.9 and 22.11: Semantic ID plus Event/SourceRef closure;
+- pib-23.5: reliability and explicit degraded state;
+- ADR-0002: `local_equivalent_real` never upgrades to actual external reality.
+
+MUST invariants:
+
+- source authority means authority over the source's own report only;
+- every core projection binds both a stable semantic claim entity and the
+  accepted EventRecord/SourceRef;
+- provenance is immutable and exact across AdapterSnapshot, EventRecord and
+  SourceRef;
+- no ack occurs before a restart-recoverable semantic postcondition exists;
+- no retry regenerates identity-bearing envelope bytes or counters.
+- every R5C-owned ID is `deterministic_derived` from a durable unversioned key;
+  R5C never calls `mintLedgerId` or `nextLedgerSequence`.
+
