+## Surprises & Discoveries
+
+- Allbuddy's first file ledger passed sequential unit tests but lost records
+  and consumed one-shot capabilities more than once under cross-process
+  concurrency.
+- A durable record still did not create a recoverable joint path: mutation
+  response loss orphaned the control/reader capability, and the browser test
+  was impersonating World by reading sessionStorage.
+- A third source implementation still failed an open review: the first run
+  response carried the first session authority, explicit abort could become
+  adoption on reload, orphaned process locks did not recover, and revision
+  operation replay returned the latest state rather than its original result.
+- The source interface therefore uses a pre-established session, exact
+  operation replay, revision-specific readback and a durable at-least-once
+  outbox. Authority delivery is part of the capability, not incidental
+  transport.
+- A fourth open review found an adoption-response race: ProductShell could
+  report abort while World still claimed adopted revision 1. The formed source
+  now represents cancel as monotonic `not_adopted@rev1` or `revoked@rev2`,
+  supersedes only unclaimed delivery, and retains ordered revision/event
+  lineage for historical backfill.
+- C4-min permits `commandIds: []` and a binding through EventRecord/source refs.
+  It does not require a World Command for an exogenous observation, but the
+  canonical NoOrphanProjection gate still requires a semantic object.
+- The current semantic store is in memory. Persisting a claim envelope is not
+  sufficient: after ack and restart, C2/C4 and all counters would disappear.
+  The World boundary therefore needs a replayable semantic journal, not merely
+  an inbox file.
+- A first open implementation review defeated a 50/50-green World adapter:
+  delta-missing still returned ack-ready, HTTP 200 with a negative ack body was
+  misconfirmed, private-invalid evidence left old success current, and Viewer
+  replay was redirectable. Two further review rounds moved authorization before
+  replay, made malformed claim/readback durable epistemic downgrades, required
+  explicit ack confirmation, repaired cut points and bound both divergence
+  candidates. These were false-closure defects, not background polish.
+- A real TCP refusal exposed a gap that fake non-2xx responses did not:
+  network rejection originally crashed the driver. The corrected real-process
+  rerun retained the source value only as offline/unknown.
+
+## Decision Log
+
+- Decision: use `local_equivalent_real`, not `external_harness` or `reference`,
+  for the external-adoption AdapterSnapshot.
+  Rationale: the episode uses a separate real local process/API and durable
+  product store, but not an independently deployed external Harness.
+
+- Decision: producer `completed`, missing first adoption readback, mismatched
+  revision/reference, wrong issuer/policy or unauthorized claim never creates
+  an adoption projection. After a previously accepted state, source
+  unavailability or gap does not advance adoption state/revision but must
+  update the existing claim projection's epistemic/sync status.
+  Rationale: those states do not establish new consumer authority, but leaving
+  an old adopted projection looking current would also be false.
+
+- Decision: one stable WorldProjection per opaque consumer reference; later
+  revisions replace its current record and emit an update delta.
+  Rationale: keeping an adopted projection beside a revoked projection would
+  leave stale success visible.
+
+- Decision: materialize one stable `claim` semantic entity per opaque source
+  reference.
+  Rationale: the entity means only “this source has a consumer-adoption
+  report”; it does not invent a Consumer, Artifact, Outcome or Effect. It
+  satisfies the semantic plus occurrence/source binding acceptance gate.
+
+- Decision: journal the complete validated lineage batch and the exact first
+  C2 envelope bytes before semantic apply or ack, then reconcile the in-memory
+  semantic store from that journal on every restart.
+  Rationale: source ack removes redelivery; durable input must be sufficient to
+  recreate the same C2/C4 current state and counters without credentials.
+
+- Decision: projection language says “consumer reports X”, never “execution
+  succeeded” or “business value realized”.
+  Rationale: Allbuddy owns adoption; neither source nor World owns correctness
+  or value Recognition.
+
+- Decision: do not alter canonical foundation, blueprint, OQ-004 or OQ-009 in
+  this experiment branch.
+  Rationale: one local episode is evidence for those decisions, not unilateral
+  resolution of them.
+
+## Context and Orientation
+
+The target package is `packages/semantic-kernel`.
+
+- `src/ingest.mjs` validates and append-only ingests C2 EventRecords.
+- `src/reference-adapter.mjs` shows how a bootstrap AdapterSnapshot is created,
+  but its `reference` provenance must not be reused for this adapter.
+- `src/outbox.mjs` shows C4 projection and SceneDelta validation.
+- `src/store.mjs` is an in-memory semantic store; the adapter's durable inbox
+  is a separate local journal boundary. Startup must replay/reconcile that
+  journal before health/read traffic or new claims so acked source facts
+  survive a World process restart.
+- `src/pipeline.mjs` remains the World-command pipeline and must not be
+  weakened. External adoption gets a separate explicit entry point.
+
+The Allbuddy source exposes:
+
+- `POST /api/external/adoption-outbox/claim` with a World bearer, `worldId` and
+  bounded lease;
+- `POST /api/external/adoption-readback` with the claimed reader handle;
+- `POST /api/external/adoption-outbox/ack` only after World persistence and
+  semantic processing.
+
+The claim response contains stable `eventId`, opaque `reference`, source
+`revision`, ordered coarse event/revision lineage, a lease-specific ack token
+and a viewer-scoped reader handle. The read request binds a lineage revision.
+The readback contains only
+`reference`, `issuer`, `policy`, `state`, `revision`, and `observedAt`.
+
+## Plan of Work
+
+### Milestone 1 — External adapter source identity
+
+Add `src/external-adoption.mjs` and a focused test file.
+
+Create an immutable per-observation `local_equivalent_real` AdapterSnapshot
+with a stable adapterId, explicit health/asOf, coverage `unknown`, capabilities
+limited to the exact external consumer-adoption claim/readback operations, and
+an honest partial reason. Do not mutate the existing reference snapshot. A
+later health observation creates a new snapshot; the adapterId's provenance
+never upgrades.
+
+Build a commandless EventRecord:
+
+- record type `REC::external.consumer_adoption`;
+- source system `allbuddy-consumer-adoption`;
+- source externalRecordId equal to stable World outbox `eventId`;
+- authority `source`, visibility `restricted`;
+- payload exactly the coarse readback;
+- sourceSequence equal to the decimal source revision;
+- no actor, task, plan, session or command correlation; `targetIds` contains
+  only the stable opaque claim entity required for the C2→C4 Source Map join;
+- later source revisions explicitly correct the previous EventRecord.
+
+Use the existing C2 ingest path and validators. Duplicate delivery is a no-op;
+conflicting content under the same source identity is rejected.
+
+AdapterSnapshot, EventRecord source executionProvenance and projection
+SourceRef executionProvenance must match exactly. A mismatch or retroactive
+reality upgrade is rejected.
+
+### Milestone 2 — Stable current projection
+
+Materialize one stable `kind: "claim"` semantic entity per opaque reference.
+Its semantics are limited to “the Allbuddy consumer-adoption source reports on
+this opaque reference.” Do not materialize a Consumer, Artifact, Outcome or
+Effect.
+
+Compile one C4 projection per claim entity. The projection has no command
+binding. Its Source Map binds the claim entity ID, current EventRecord and
+external-adoption AdapterSnapshot/SourceRef, declares the compiler rule and
+content version, and records AWIR/projection versions. The narrative and state
+modifiers say only that the Allbuddy consumer source reports the coarse state
+and revision.
+
+On revision `n+1`, require or backfill accepted revision `n` from the claimed
+lineage, ingest a correction EventRecord, replace the existing projection with
+the same projection ID and emit an `updated` SceneDelta. A stale, skipped,
+unbackfillable or conflicting revision produces no authoritative adoption
+state/revision advance; an existing claim projection still receives the
+required stale/unknown/disputed epistemic update.
+
+Projection identity derives only from the stable claim entity ID plus a fixed,
+unversioned identity rule. Compiler content versions never change projection
+ID. Replacement filters the prior same-ID row, inserts exactly one replacement
+and validates the complete C4 current store before commit; it never appends
+divergent rows under one ID. `SceneDelta.updated` carries the projection ref
+only; consumers read replacement content from the current projection store.
+History remains in C2.
+
+Failure presentation is explicit:
+
+- unauthorized/malformed/private responses fail closed and create no business
+  projection or existence leak;
+- first unavailable observation creates no adoption projection, only adapter
+  health/freshness evidence;
+- after a last-known state, offline/stale/unbackfillable gaps preserve that
+  state as last-known but downgrade sync/epistemic modifiers to
+  stale/unknown/partial/offline;
+- same-revision divergence or incompatible valid lineage preserves dispute
+  evidence and marks the current claim projection disputed. Because the
+  conflicting source candidate cannot enter ordinary C2 under the same
+  externalRecordId, World emits a deterministic
+  `REC::reconciliation.external_consumer_adoption_conflict` EventRecord with
+  `authority: "reconciliation"` containing only source refs, revision/event
+  identities and a canonical ordered digest pair, never candidate private
+  bodies. This is a World reconciliation output, not an Allbuddy-authored
+  report. It uses the same per-observation `local_equivalent_real` adoption
+  AdapterSnapshot, a deterministic conflict externalRecordId derived from
+  reference + revision + ordered digest pair, and an explicit World
+  reconciliation sourceSystem. The disputed projection Source Map binds this
+  reconciliation record;
+- source-confirmed/in-sync returns only after complete contiguous lineage and
+  readbacks revalidate.
+
+### Milestone 3 — Recoverable World journal and claim/persist/ack
+
+Add a file journal that is sufficient to recreate the accepted C2/C4 state
+after source ack and World restart. For each claimed reference it persists:
+
+- canonical immutable claim core: eventId, reference, revision and ordered
+  eventId/revision lineage;
+- every strict coarse readback in the contiguous lineage prefix;
+- the exact immutable external AdapterSnapshot envelope bytes used by those
+  EventRecords, including stable adapterId, snapshot ID, asOf, health,
+  capabilities, coverage, partial reason and provenance;
+- the first complete C2 envelope bytes, including fixed first-seen timestamps;
+- stable claim entity/projection identity allocation;
+- processing phase:
+  `staged | semantically_applied | ack_pending | ack_confirmed`;
+- the semantic ack-ready postcondition and counters needed for deterministic
+  replay.
+
+The same journal also persists non-claim state transitions that have no source
+ack:
+
+- immutable AdapterSnapshot/health observation envelope bytes;
+- affected reference and ordered epistemic/sync transition;
+- deterministic reconciliation/dispute EventRecord envelope;
+- the resulting projection/delta postcondition and counters.
+
+Startup replays accepted lineage batches and later health/reconciliation
+observations in their durable order. An offline or disputed projection must
+remain offline/disputed after restart until a newer complete source validation
+is journaled; replaying an older accepted batch must never upgrade it.
+
+The current memory store has no ledger-counter restore API. Therefore adapter,
+per-observation AdapterSnapshot, claim entity, projection, reconciliation
+EventRecord and SceneDelta IDs all derive deterministically from journaled
+unversioned keys and never use the ledger sequence namespace. Replay rebuilds
+AWIR revision and per-viewer scene revision in journal order: it verifies each
+journaled pre/post counter and calls `nextAwirRevision` or
+`nextSceneRevision` exactly once only when the corresponding full postcondition
+is absent. Exact replay performs no counter advance.
+
+Journal publishing uses constrained eventId filenames, canonical
+serialization, 0600 temporary files, file fsync, exclusive publish/atomic
+rename, directory fsync and orphan/truncation recovery.
+
+Transport authority is deliberately ephemeral. World bearer, lease token and
+reader readCapability never enter durable journal, EventRecord, projection,
+logs or evidence. Re-lease may change token/handle. eventId dedupe compares
+only canonical immutable core; a changed reference/revision/lineage is
+divergent, while token rotation is normal.
+
+On startup, before health/read traffic or a new claim, replay journal entries
+in stable reference/revision order and reconcile the fresh in-memory semantic
+store to their complete postconditions.
+
+Add an injectable-fetch poll-cycle function:
+
+1. claim with the ephemeral World credential;
+2. canonicalize and fsync the immutable claim core;
+3. validate a unique eventId per revision and contiguous ordered lineage;
+4. read every missing lineage revision in ascending order;
+5. validate and durably stage the complete batch before any C2/C4 exposure;
+6. reconcile/apply the full semantic postcondition;
+7. verify ack-ready: all exact EventRecords exist, the stable claim entity and
+   projection point to the claimed current revision, and required deltas are
+   committed;
+8. ack with the current lease token.
+
+If rev2 arrives first, rev1 and rev2 are both read and staged before either is
+visible. A read failure yields zero business-state mutation and no ack.
+Duplicate C2 alone never means the full semantic operation succeeded:
+reconciliation repairs C2-only, C4-only or delta-missing cut points before ack.
+
+A crash before durable stage does not ack. A crash after stage replays the
+batch. A crash after ack rebuilds C2/C4 from the journal without source
+redelivery. If ack response is lost, a new claim supplies a new ephemeral token
+whose immutable core must match the journal.
+
+### Milestone 4 — Tests and real episode
+
+Tests must cover:
+
+- adopted revision 1 creates one claim semantic entity, one commandless
+  EventRecord and one semantically bound projection;
+- producer-only or missing readback creates neither;
+- wrong issuer/policy/reference/revision/state shape creates neither;
+- private sentinel/additional fields are rejected rather than copied;
+- exact claim replay is idempotent;
+- an active lease cannot be concurrently reclaimed by another process using
+  the same `worldId`, and an expired lease gets a new ack token;
+- lease-token/reader-capability rotation leaves canonical durable bytes equal;
+- same eventId divergent delivery is rejected;
+- response/read/ack failure leaves delivery unacked;
+- World crash before and after local persistence converges to one inbox record;
+- revision 2 revocation corrects revision 1, updates the same projection ID and
+  removes stale adopted presentation;
+- a delivery whose unclaimed revision 1 was superseded by revision 2 backfills
+  both historical readbacks in one cycle, exposes only revoked as current, and
+  retains the adopted → revoked source lineage;
+- skipped/stale revision and duplicate update operation do not advance World;
+- wrong viewer/bearer cannot expose existence through the adapter result.
+- same-revision divergence produces disputed evidence and no state advance;
+- post-confirmation source offline/gap downgrades the current projection to
+  last-known stale/unknown rather than leaving adopted looking current;
+- AdapterSnapshot/EventRecord/SourceRef provenance mismatch or retroactive
+  reality upgrade is rejected;
+- C2 retry reuses the exact persisted envelope even when wall clock changes;
+- ack-then-restart with no source redelivery reconstructs the same claim entity,
+  EventRecord IDs, projection ID/current state and semantic counters;
+- a cut-point matrix at persist, final read, C2 commit, projection replacement,
+  delta commit, ack send and lost ack response converges without duplicate
+  revision/counter advance;
+- two references replayed in reverse order retain their own stable IDs and
+  revisions.
+- ack/restart followed by a new source revision creates collision-free
+  deterministic IDs and exactly one required AWIR/scene counter advance;
+- after a journaled offline or disputed update, kill/restart without source
+  recovery preserves the same projection ID and stale/offline or disputed
+  state; accepted lineage replay cannot restore in-sync/source-confirmed.
+
+Test ownership is explicit:
+
+- semantic-kernel unit tests use injected fake fetch only for World parsing,
+  journal, reducer, reconciliation and ack-order behavior;
+- active lease exclusion, token rotation, wrong bearer/viewer
+  non-enumeration, source cancellation and privacy are source-owned
+  integration claims and must be tested against the actual local Allbuddy HTTP
+  process in the cross-repository episode;
+- the final evidence matrix never treats a fake-fetch World test as proof of
+  Allbuddy authorization or process isolation.
+
+Then run a real local Allbuddy server and an independent World process using
+explicit synthetic credentials and stable temporary stores. Save only redacted
+readback, World inbox metadata, EventRecord IDs, projection IDs/states and test
+outputs.
+
+## Validation and Acceptance
+
+Use Node 24 for all World commands:
+
+    PATH=/opt/homebrew/opt/node@24/bin:$PATH node --version
+    PATH=/opt/homebrew/opt/node@24/bin:$PATH pnpm --filter @agent-world/semantic-kernel test
+    PATH=/opt/homebrew/opt/node@24/bin:$PATH pnpm --filter @agent-world/awir-schema test:contracts
+    PATH=/opt/homebrew/opt/node@24/bin:$PATH bash scripts/verify-package.sh
+
+Acceptance requires:
+
+- independent semantic, systems and feasibility reviewers approve the revised
+  plan;
+- no existing command pipeline or canonical schema is weakened;
+- real claim/persist/read/process/ack occurs across separate Allbuddy and World
+  processes;
+- the World projection survives replay and follows revocation;
+- producer-only, unauthorized and first-unavailable ablations emit no adoption
+  projection; unavailability after a prior accepted state emits only the
+  required stale/unknown epistemic update and never advances adoption
+  state/revision;
+- no source bearer, private Artifact content, query, raw tenant or sentinel is
+  present in World semantic records or evidence.
+- source ack occurs only after the durable journal can recreate the exact
+  semantic postcondition on a fresh memory store;
+- no evidence text exceeds the scoped synthetic-source conclusion or implies
+  human/customer adoption, execution success or business value.
+
+## Idempotence and Recovery
+
+All operations are safe to rerun against fresh temporary stores. The journal
+is at-least-once: a canonically identical immutable event core is accepted,
+divergent identity/lineage is quarantined, and ephemeral token changes are
+ignored. C2 ingest dedupes only the exact persisted EventRecord envelope.
+Reconciliation treats the same accepted source revision as no counter advance
+but verifies and repairs its full C2/C4/delta postcondition before ack.
+
+If implementation fails, delete only files introduced by this plan in the
+isolated worktree. Do not reset, stash, clean, rewrite history or touch the
+user's source checkout.
+
+## Artifacts and Notes
+
+Expected implementation files:
+
+- `packages/semantic-kernel/src/external-adoption.mjs`
+- `packages/semantic-kernel/test/external-adoption.test.mjs`
+- `packages/semantic-kernel/scripts/run-external-adoption.mjs`, an independent
+  process entrypoint that imports only the package export, receives base URL,
+  journal path, worldId and credentials through explicit local arguments/env,
+  replays the journal before polling, and emits redacted JSON evidence
+- package export updates if the real process driver needs them
+
+Expected research evidence lives outside this repository in the isolated
+Harness research worktree. No bearer or private Artifact body is copied there.
+
+## Interfaces and Dependencies
+
+The module should export narrowly named functions equivalent to:
+
+    createExternalAdoptionAdapterSnapshot(store, { now })
+    stageExternalAdoptionBatch(journalDirectory, claimCore, readbacks, options)
+    reconcileExternalAdoptionJournal(store, journalDirectory, options)
+    applyExternalAdoptionReadbacks(store, stagedBatch, options)
+    runExternalAdoptionPollCycle(options)
+
+The poller must read exactly the revision named by the claimed delivery and
+every missing predecessor named by lineage, then ack with that delivery's
+ephemeral lease token. All network access is injected through `fetchImpl`. All
+semantic writes go through existing store ports and C2/C4 validators.
+File-system writes are confined to the explicit World journal directory.
+Because the current C4 validator does not cross-check SourceRef provenance
+against AdapterSnapshot, the module must implement and test the full custom
+join before commit: EventRecord adapterSnapshotId resolves; EventRecord
+adapterId equals snapshot.adapterId.canonical; EventRecord provenance equals
+snapshot provenance; and projection SourceRef snapshot, provenance,
+sourceSystem and any externalRecordId/checksum equal the bound current
+EventRecord.
+
+## Outcomes & Retrospective
+
+The scoped local implementation is complete. It adds a public package seam,
+0600 fsynced immutable journals, exact C2/C4/delta replay, one stable opaque
+claim entity and projection, explicit offline/stale/disputed observations,
+source-to-target Viewer authorization, and a separate process driver.
+
+Verification at the final implementation cutoff:
+
+- semantic-kernel: 58/58;
+- AWIR contracts: 191/191;
+- `scripts/verify-package.sh`: PASS;
+- Allbuddy: typecheck PASS, 8 files / 49 tests PASS, targeted lint PASS;
+- prior real ProductShell browser race/recovery suite: 1/1 PASS.
+
+The real cross-repository episode used separate Allbuddy and World processes.
+One projection followed `adopted@rev1 → revoked@rev2 → offline/unknown →
+adopted@rev3`, survived source ack and fresh World replay, and contained no
+Artifact/query/tenant/capability bytes. Producer-only and wrong-bearer
+ablations yielded no projection. A pre-frozen separate `drawing-retrieval`
+holdout predicted and obtained `not_adopted@rev1` with stable restart IDs.
+
+This establishes only that an independent local World
+transport/materialization preserved a synthetic local Allbuddy source report.
+It does not establish human/customer adoption, Artifact correctness, execution
+success, business value, production identity, multi-host durability, or
+persistence for the rest of Agent World.
+
+Five unseeded implementation re-review rounds were required after the first
+green implementation. The final reviewer reproduced the full-journal revision
+identity preflight, observed zero mutation on a conflicting durable set, found
+no new scoped load-bearing Defeater, and returned PASS for this local claim.
